<p>These keybindings are good to know when working with a mouse in Emacs.</p>
<p><code>F10</code> (<code>menu-bar-open</code>) :: Start key navigation of the menu bar in FRAME.</p>
<p><code>S-F10</code> (<code>context-menu-open</code>) :: Start key navigation of the context menu. This needs <code>context-menu-mode</code> enabled.</p>
<p><code>C-x z</code> (<code>repeat</code>) :: Repeat most recently executed command. Yes, <code>repeat</code> works also for commands issued via mouse too!</p>
<p>Knowing that <code>repeat</code> works with menu commands (both main and context) is particularly useful with the additions to the main menu made by the latest <a href="https://github.com/kickingvegas/anju/discussions/63">Anju v1.2.0 update</a>. Shown below is a demo of using “Duplicate” (<code>duplicate-dwim</code>) from the Edit menu, then using <code>C-x z</code> and then <code>z</code> successively to repeat the duplication.</p>
